## Why This Is Asked
Tests classic DP with an additional dimension (at most k intervals) and reconstruction—a common pattern in scheduling optimization problems.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with a cardinality constraint (at most k intervals)
- Predecessor p(i) computed via binary search on sorted end times
- DP table with an extra dimension tracking the number of selected intervals
- Backtracking reconstruction to output the chosen jobs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueKJobs(jobs, k) {
  const sorted = jobs.map((j, idx) => ({ ...j, idx })).sort((a, b) => a.end - b.end);
  const n = sorted.length;
  const ends = sorted.map(j => j.end);

  const p = (i) => {
    let lo = 0, hi = i - 1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
      const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);
      if (ends[mid] <= sorted[i].start) lo = mid + 1;
      else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return hi;
  };

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const prev = p(i - 1) + 1;
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][t], dp[prev][t - 1] + sorted[i - 1].value);
    }
  }

  const selected = [];
  let t = k;
  for (let i = n; i > 0 && t > 0; i--) {
    if (dp[i][t] !== dp[i - 1][t]) {
      selected.push(sorted[i - 1]);
      t--;
    }
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], jobs: selected.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to derive a tree DP with multiple subtrees and an exact count constraint. Requires knapsack-style merging across children and careful reconstruction to report all k endpoints. Also checks edge-disjointness handling and correctness when k exceeds leaves.

## Key Concepts

- Tree DP with per-node knapsack merge
- Exact-path counting and edge-disjointness
- Result reconstruction: path endpoints
- Complexity reasoning: O(n k^2) time, O(n k) space

## Code Example

```javascript
function dfs(u, k, val, children, dp) {
  let f = Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity);
  f[0] = 0;
  for (const v of children[u]) {
    let g = Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity);
    for (let i = 0; i <= k; i++) {
      if (f[i] <= -Infinity) continue;
      for (let t = 0; t + i <= k; t++) {
        g[i+t] = Math.max(g[i+t], f[i] + dp[v][t]);
      }
    }
    f = g;
  }
  for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) dp[u][t] = f[t] + t * val[u];
}
```

